# Cross-origin isolation headers for static hosts that honour a `_headers` file
# (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify). Vite copies `public/` to the dist root, so this
# ships as `dist/_headers`.
#
# These enable `crossOriginIsolated` (SharedArrayBuffer), which the OPTIONAL
# Steam Audio backend (`?engine=steam`) needs for its threaded reflection sim.
# The DEFAULT game engine does NOT need these headers and runs fine without them;
# only `?engine=steam` requires them and otherwise falls back to the default engine.
#
# Hosts that do NOT support `_headers` must send the same two headers via their own
# server/CDN config (see docs/DEPLOY.md).
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
